FIELD 1 - LITERALLY MEASURED
----------------------------

A. Proxy network and instrumental target

The paper describes a multiproxy network of annual-resolution dendroclimatic,
ice-core/ice-melt, coral, historical, precipitation, and instrumental records.
It reports 112 indicators back to 1820. The instrumental calibration field contains
1,082 nearly continuous land-air/sea-surface temperature grid-point series for
1902-1995, and the proxy calibration interval is 1902-1980.

Source locator:
- MBH98, Nature pp. 779-780, "Data" and "Multiproxy calibration."
- PDF text lines 51-89 and 94-116.
- Target PDF: https://www.meteo.psu.edu/holocene/public_html/shared/articles/mbh98.pdf

B. Backward-declining networks and reconstructive scope

Reported network sizes and retained skill:
- 112 indicators from 1820
- 93 from 1760
- 74 from 1700
- 57 from 1600
- 24 from 1450
- 22 from 1400

At 1400, only the first eigenvector is resolved, associated with approximately
40-50% of NH variance in calibration and verification. The paper says networks
before 1400 show little evidence of skill even for that eigenvector.

Source locator:
- MBH98, Nature pp. 781-782.
- PDF text lines 220-285.

C. Calibration, verification, and uncertainty construction

The calibration uses PCA/eigenvectors of the instrumental field, fits proxy indicators
against retained principal components over 1902-1980, then reconstructs annual
principal components and temperature fields backward in time. Verification includes
a 219-grid-point 1854-1901 data set. The paper calculates reconstruction uncertainty
by assuming unresolved variance is Gaussian distributed over time; the variance and
error bars expand backward as the proxy network thins.

Source locator:
- MBH98, Nature pp. 780-782 and Methods pp. 785-787.
- PDF text lines 166-219, 557 onward, especially lines 760-795.
- Figure 5 and caption, Nature p. 783.

